import io

P = r"C:\dev\blog\death-of-software\projects\strehl\docs\research\SYNTHESIS.md"
SRC = "IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e)"

NEW_FACTS = """| 1983 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **THE DEFAULT MERGE KEPT SINGLE-FRAME NOISE WHERE IT SHOULD AVERAGE, AND A PER-FRAME GATE CANNOT FIX IT.** On `bee-3-cpl` a 150-frame half stack carried 1.11x the luma noise of a single frame where averaging would give 0.08x: over 150-300 frames some frame clears a per-frame noise gate at almost every coefficient (multiple comparisons), and the frame selected is the noisiest. The shipped **ensemble gate** (`MergeConfig::ensemble`, default on) judges each coefficient's frames together -- dominance of the strongest frame over the others, coherence, and a wide-area coherence, against measured nulls -- and blends toward the plain mean only where every test reads noise. Against synthetic truth it lowered error power in 176 of 180 cells (worst +1.9%, coarse band at an occluder boundary). |
| 1984 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **HALO BESIDE BRIGHT EDGES CAME FROM COARSE BANDS SELECTING ON ENERGY THAT BARELY DEPENDS ON FOCUS, AND FROM A PLAIN-MEAN BASE.** On `high-res-calibration-slide-2-cpl` the dark ground beside bright bars read +35% over an in-focus composite. **Pooled evidence** (each band selects on the mean of its own and every finer band's energy in noise units) plus a base band **weighted** by the coarsest band's selection took that to +14.5%; the remaining 16-64 px excess was the tone curve, not the merge (scene-linear masters show none). Finer-only evidence (+11%) was rejected because coarse texture lost. |
| 1985 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **WITH POOLED EVIDENCE THE COARSEST EXPONENT SHOULD BE 4, NOT 2, AND FINER LEVELS SHOULD COUNT 2X PER OCTAVE.** Synthetic truth, 120 cells: coarse exponent 4 geo-mean error 0.930 of exponent 2 (10/120 cells worse, worst 1.037); pooled ratio 2 a further 0.922 (1/120 worse, worst 1.037), with 2.5-4 losing coarse texture. On `bug-4` the glow 8 px beside a bright iridescent edge went 195 (previous default) to 100 against 52 in the frame focused there (1e-3 linear). Burst truth unchanged within 0.3% except coarse flat -14%. |
| 1986 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **GLINT TAMING MUST JUDGE A GLINT AGAINST THE LIT SUBJECT, NOT A MEAN THAT INCLUDES A DARK BACKDROP.** The development control compressed light more than 2 stops above its cell's typical level; on rutile over hematite whole golden blades read as glints and were dimmed. When the luminance histogram splits (Otsu) into populations at least 3.5 stops apart, each cell's level is now the lit slices' mean, pulled toward the whole cell's mean by 5% of its population: blades keep their level (0.4-0.6 bin 0.938 -> 0.999 of untreated), peacock and garnet recipes are byte-identical. Rejected on the way: fading by colour, a size share, and a prior toward the image's lit mean (it stopped taming glints on a dark stone beside a large bright area). |
| 1987 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **FUSING EACH SOURCE'S RECONSTRUCTED RGB INSTEAD OF RE-MOSAICING IS REJECTED.** +1-4 dB on a synthetic, but on the neutral razor high-frequency chroma rose 1.48-1.57x and on `109MSDCF` chroma noise rose 1.8x: the second MHC demosaic acts as a chroma low-pass that the RGB path loses. |
| 1988 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **FOUR OCCLUSION RULES FAILED TO REMOVE THE BEE-3 ANTENNA SEE-THROUGH GHOST WITHOUT HARM.** A coarse-consistency gate against a reference render (changed 1.1% of pixels, streaks unchanged: the reference carries them); a depth-ordered occlusion prior (\"within 1/8\" of the best focus score removed the ghost and softened porous hair; \"within 1/2\" changed nothing); a streaming first-significant-frame rule (zsig 8 and 4: same softening); and a light-agreement opacity cue (changed at most 0.85% of pixels, antenna interior unchanged). A hair mat is porous, and the antenna is wide enough to stay dark in the frames that draw the ghost. Open: an opacity estimate. Pooled evidence makes the ghost slightly more contrasty (antenna-strip 99th percentile 59 -> 61). |
| 1989 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **THE SHIPPED LATERAL-CA CONSTANTS ARE WRONG PER CAPTURE, IN SCALE AND IN AN UNAPPLIED TRANSLATION.** Measured on output residuals, red's native scale ran -258 to -611 ppm across seven captures against -508 shipped (over-corrected by 75-250 ppm on natural subjects), and red and blue carry a translation of up to 0.3 px. Fact 1570's prediction (per-capture estimation, never a constant) holds. Raw single-frame estimates are not reliable enough (on rutile one frame gave the right scale and a wrong translation). |
| 1990 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **PER-CAPTURE LATERAL-CA REFINEMENT IS SHIPPED, DEFAULT ON.** A preview of every Nth frame (frames/32 clamped to 1..8) is merged, the red and blue displacement against green is measured on its white-balanced **mosaic** with each colour interpolated from its own sites only (a demosaic that borrows green's detail under-reads it: measured on an MHC demosaic it left about half of bug-4's red residual), and the render uses the profile plus that residual. Neutral-target edge fringing: slide-2 7.343% -> 2.965% red, 5.371% -> 2.108% blue; razor 4.069% -> 3.782% red. bug-4 red residual +250 -> +10 ppm. Preview 15-18 s against an 84-93 s render. Skipped with no matching profile, `--fix-ca=off`, alignment off or binned output. |
| 1991 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **THE CA ESTIMATOR IS A WINDOWED PHASE CORRELATION OF GRADIENT MAGNITUDE, STRUCTURE-WEIGHTED; THE ALTERNATIVES LOST ON NEUTRAL TARGETS.** Rendering each estimator's correction and scoring slide-2 fringe: Python instrument 3.154% red; Rust gradient energy + iterative solve 3.554%; intensity matching with a per-tile gain 10.028% (worse than shipped). An iterative Lucas-Kanade solve read fractional shifts 4-10% high on planted shifts (interpolation locking). A tile gate on normalised cross-correlation was a wash (peacock -53 -> -14 ppm but opal -27 -> +67 ppm) and was not shipped. |
| 1992 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **A PER-CHANNEL FOCUS OFFSET FOR LONGITUDINAL CA IS REAL AND STILL REJECTED.** Red and blue focus nearer than green: -1.92 / -1.86 frames on the flat slide, -0.84 / -0.62 on `bee-3-cpl`, -1.08 / -0.40 on slide-2. Folding red and blue from the offset frame helped the flat slide once lateral CA was refined (red fringe 2.542% -> 2.010%) but fringed far more on slide-2 (2.965% -> 10.341%) and the razor (3.782% -> 6.052%). ARGUED cause: channels from another frame inherit that frame's placement error relative to green's, while within a frame all channels share it. Proposed as cheap in fact 1417; now measured. |
| 1993 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **SESSION FUSION DOES NOT GAIN FROM THE ORDINARY MERGE'S NEW SELECTION, EVEN WITH THE ENSEMBLE GATE.** Ported and parity-tested against the ordinary merge (max difference < 0.01), the gate is nearly neutral on the bug-4 session (1231 frames; noise 0.842 -> 0.840, black 1.573 -> 1.594), and the full selection raises black 11% (1.573 -> 1.747) and the glow 8-16 px from bright edges to 1.163x. Sessions keep their selection. The lateral-CA refinement does carry over through a session preview: red +212 -> -10 ppm, blue -196 -> -32 ppm. |
| 1994 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **WITH THE WEIGHTED BASE AS DEFAULT, EXPERIMENTAL TEMPORAL SMOOTHING REFUSED EVERY RENDER UNTIL IT WAS GIVEN THE MEAN BASE.** The temporal guide's preflight accepts only the mean base band; the desktop compiles the feature, so every stack with \"Temporal detail smoothing\" on failed after fact 1984. Temporal renders now use the mean base (and so do not get its halo reduction), and the CA preview never runs the temporal path. |
| 1995 | MEASURED | IQ-2026-11-02 (`experiments/image-quality-2026-11-02/results.md` @ f16e3e0e) | **MULTI-STACK SESSIONS ARE MOVED BEHIND THE OFF-BY-DEFAULT `multi-stack` BUILD FEATURE (OWNER DECISION).** The `session` subcommand, the session engine and the desktop's session actions are absent from default builds; specification types and folder discovery stay compiled so saved results open. |
"""


def main():
    with io.open(P, encoding="utf-8") as f:
        text = f.read()
    assert "| 1983 |" not in text, "facts 1983+ already allocated"
    anchor = "| 1982 |"
    assert text.count(anchor) == 1
    i = text.index(anchor)
    j = text.index("\n", i) + 1
    text = text[:j] + NEW_FACTS + text[j:]
    for n in range(1983, 1996):
        row = [l for l in text.split("\n") if l.startswith(f"| {n} |")]
        assert len(row) == 1, n
        k = row[0].count("|") - row[0].count("\\|")
        assert k == 5, f"fact {n}: {k} unescaped pipes"
    with io.open(P, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
        f.write(text)
    print("folded facts 1983-1995 after fact 1982")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
